course: dictionary
lesson: 10533
title: Making things uglier
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Uglify» means to make something ugly, or uglier. The root word is ugly, and the -ify ending turns it into an action: to uglify something is to do something that makes it less pretty.
explain: The Gryphon in Alice's story asks if she knows what «beautify» is. Alice says doubtfully «it means—to—make—anything—prettier», so «uglify» must mean the opposite. When you meet a new word, look for a clue like this: a word that is explained or set against an opposite.
explain: This word is rare and a little playful. You might meet it in a story, or in a complaint about a building or place spoilt by ugly changes. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "The huge new sign will uglify the old village" only makes sense if uglify means to make ugly.
fact: Uglify is a verb: uglify, uglifies, uglified, uglifying.
fact: «Uglify» means to make something ugly or uglier.
fact: The opposite of uglify is «beautify», which means to make something prettier.
fact: In computing, «uglify» means squashing program code so it is shorter and hard to read.
fact: Because the word is rare, you may need to use the clues around it, such as an opposite word, to work out its meaning.
exercise: «The Gryphon asked Alice if she knew what beautify means.» What does beautify mean? | To squash something small | To lose something | *To make something prettier | To make something ugly
exercise: Alice thinks beautify means to make anything prettier. What must uglify mean, since it is the opposite? | *To make something uglier | To make something quieter | To make something bigger | To make something wetter
exercise: A council plans a new car park that will uglify the old park. What does uglify mean here? | *Make it uglier | Make it busier | Make it wetter | Make it cleaner
exercise: Find and copy the word from the lesson that is the opposite of uglify. | context | verb | *beautify | ugly
test: Which word is the opposite of uglify? | Ugly | *Beautify | Ancient | Squash
test: In computing, what does uglify do to program code? | *Squashes it so it is shorter and harder to read | Sends it to a printer | Makes it longer and easier to read | Turns it into a picture
exam: Which sentence uses uglify correctly? | The gardeners will beautify the park with roses | The children will uglify their smiles | *The new billboards will uglify the old village | The rain will uglify the sunny sky
